│ The issue is caused by a race condition where _is_session_active   │
│ returns True even though the session is effectively closed or      │
│ shutting down (due to a closed _close_future), leading to          │
│ scheduling calls on an event loop that is no longer able to handle │
│ them, which results in indefinite hanging on 4xx/5xx errors.       │
│                                                                    │
│ The proposed fix is to enhance the _is_session_active method such  │
│ that it not only checks whether the background thread is alive but │
│ also whether the _close_future is still pending. If _close_future  │
│ is done, it means the session is closing or closed, so the method  │
│ should return False.                                               │
│                                                                    │
│ This patch minimally modifies only the _is_session_active method   │
│ with the additional check.                                         │
